    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2e0f583e56571e6b87487cff14c8d48386b765cc09ba0b057e69323fd328ee78",
      "text": "Day 5 · Early-morning excursion to the El Tatio Geysers, at more than 4,000 m: at sunrise, roughly from 06:00 to 07:00, more than 70 fumaroles send up jets of steam and form pools of boiling water, white against the deep blue sky. A warming breakfast amid the geysers, where morning temperatures can drop to −2 °C, then a swim for those who wish in a natural thermal pool. Return to San Pedro to rest.\n\nIn the afternoon, an excursion to the Moon Valley, in the Cordillera de la Sal within Los Flamencos National Reserve: salt ridges, dunes and rock formations shaped by wind and water over millions of years. Watch the sunset from a viewpoint as the rocks turn red, orange and purple.\n\nAccommodation: Nayara Alto Atacama, Tilo Suite, breakfast",
